            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What warranty comes with the Unsit?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                iMovR's warranty section, provided by InMovement, lists a lifetime frame, two years on parts and one year of labour, matching an independent review. The same page also shows a 3-year motor badge and a 10-year motors-and-electronics statement. The lifetime frame is consistent; confirm the rest in writing. The Lander desk has its own warranty.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying an Unsit Treadmill Desk</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The Unsit is a specialised machine, and most regrets come from the desk, the delivery or the paperwork rather than the treadmill.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ordering a desk that is too narrow or too low</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The Unsit needs at least 40 inches between the desk's lifting columns, and a 53-inch or wider desktop on iMovR's desks. Standing on a 5-inch deck also needs a desk about five inches higher than your standing height. Check both, and ask iMovR to confirm the height range for your exact Lander frame and top, since its listings differ.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Taking the highest weight figure on the page</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">iMovR's Unsit page states 300, 350 and 400 lb in different places. A buyer near the top of that range who relies on 400 could find the rated figure is 300. Ask for the limit in writing, and ask whether exceeding it affects the warranty, before you order.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Choosing kerbside delivery for an upstairs office</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Free kerbside delivery leaves a 162 lb, 39-inch-wide machine on your driveway. Getting it up stairs and through doors takes several people. Price inside delivery ($249) or white-glove installation ($499) against the help you have, and measure doorways first.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Throwing away the pallet</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">The 30-day return requires written authorisation, the original carton and the original pallet, and return freight costs you $280 to $500. Keep all of the packaging until you are sure, and walk on the machine at your normal pace for full working sessions in the first days so any problem shows up in time.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

